.Im MicroEmacs command|games
.so me.tni
.TH Balls 3
.XI Balls - "\*(mS bouncing ball playground"
.SH NAME
Balls \- \*(mS bouncing ball playground
.Me $a
.SH SYNOPSIS
.na
\fBBalls\fR
.ad
.SH DESCRIPTION
A  playground  rather  than a game \- there is  nothing  to win.  Balls  fall,
bounce off the walls and floor,  roll,  come to rest,  and  optionally  bounce
off  each  other.  Up to 100 balls  may be in the air at once.
.PP
Almost  everything  about the  simulation  can be changed  while it is running:
the  strength  and  direction  of  gravity,  how much  speed a ball  keeps when
it  bounces,  whether  balls  collide  with one  another,  and  whether  there
is a bat to knock them about with.  The  current  settings  are  shown  along
the status line, together with the frame rate.
.PP
Balls  may be picked up and thrown by hand.  Hold  \fBbutton 1\fR  over a ball
to  grab  it,  move  the  pointer,  and  let  go \- the ball  leaves  with the
speed of the throw.  \fBButton 3\fR  drops a new ball  wherever  the  pointer
is.
.PP
The  pointer  may  also be  turned  into a lump of  gravity  of its own with
\fBa\fR,  either  pulling  the balls  towards  it or  pushing  them  away.
.SH KEYS
The keys used to control \fBBalls\fR are:
.IP "\fB?\fR or \fBh\fR"
Show or hide the key help.
.IP \fBspace\fR
Cycle the bat: off, across, upright, off.
.IP "\fBn\fR or \fBx\fR"
Add or remove a ball.
.IP \fBs\fR
Change the size of the next ball added: any size, tiny, small, medium, large.
.IP \fBr\fR
Reset, back to the starting set of balls.
.IP \fBp\fR
Pause.
.IP \fB.\fR
Run a single frame, for watching a collision resolve.
.IP \fBa\fR
The pointer as a lump of gravity: off, pull, push, off.
.IP "\fB\-\fR or \fB=\fR"
Weaken or strengthen that pull.  \fB+\fR does the same as \fB=\fR.
.IP \fBg\fR
Cycle gravity: normal, moon, none, upside down.
.IP \fBwheel\fR
Trim gravity, one unit a click.
.IP "\fB[\fR or \fB]\fR"
Less or more bounce.
.IP \fBc\fR
Ball to ball collisions on or off.
.IP "\fBbutton 1\fR"
Drag a ball to pick it up, let go to throw it.
.IP "\fBbutton 3\fR"
Drop a new ball under the pointer.
.IP "\fBq\fR, \fBesc\fR or \fBC-g\fR"
Quit.
.SH NOTES
\fBBalls\fR is a macro defined in \fCballs.emf\fR.
.PP
The  simulation  runs in  whatever  room  the  window  gives  it and  adjusts
if the window is resized.  Adding a great many balls with  collisions  turned
on will lower the frame rate.
